# .trivyignore — Trivy vulnerability exceptions for dineOS
#
# POLICY (DO-9)
# ─────────────
# This file exists solely for justified false positives — CVEs that have been
# reviewed and confirmed to pose no real risk in the dineOS runtime context.
# It is NOT a place to defer remediation of real vulnerabilities.
#
# Every entry MUST have:
#   1. A comment block with Reason, Scope, Added, and Review fields (see template below).
#   2. The native Trivy expiry suffix  exp:YYYY-MM-DD  on the CVE line itself.
#      Trivy treats an expired entry as if it were not present, so the vulnerability
#      will re-appear in scan results when the review date passes.
#   3. A maximum review window of 90 days from the Added date.
#
# TEMPLATE (copy this block for each new entry)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# # CVE-YYYY-NNNNN — <one-line description of the vulnerability>
# # Reason:   <why this does not apply to dineOS in production>
# #           <cite the upstream advisory or vendor statement if available>
# # Scope:    <which image(s) and/or path(s) this applies to>
# # Added:    YYYY-MM-DD by <GitHub username>
# # Review:   YYYY-MM-DD  (must be ≤ 90 days from Added)
# CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# REVIEW PROCESS
# ──────────────
# See docs/devops/security.md §"Vulnerability Exceptions (.trivyignore)" for
# the full add / review / expiry workflow.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NO ACTIVE EXCEPTIONS
# All scans are currently passing without suppressions.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
